The following conditions are imposed on the provider's registration under s 29 of the National Vocational Education and Training Regulator Act 2011:

i. The Registered Training Organisation (RTO) is not permitted to amend its scope of VET registration until such time as a post&minus;initial audit has been completed;

ii. The RTO must retain copies of all completed student assessment material and material used to assess recognised prior learning for the entire period of its initial registration;

iii. The RTO is required to monitor and record attendance for all students and retain those records for the entire period of its initial registration;

iv. The RTO is to notify the Australian Skills Quality Authority (ASQA) at least 14 days prior to the sale of the RTO, the identity and contact details of any purchaser, for the entire period of its initial registration;

v. The RTO is to notify ASQA of the name, units of competency engaged to deliver and contact details of any trainer or assessor it engages or ceases to engage within 14 days of the event for the entire period of its initial registration.

